      "title": "College overlap framework",
      "kind": "note",
      "count": null,
      "credits": null,
      "credit_unit": "unknown",
      "category": "other",
      "source_id": "columbia-ai-minor-college-policies",
      "source_text": null,
      "summary": "Eligible shared foundational skills include elementary/intermediate languages, the listed calculus sequences, STAT UN1101/UN1201 and COMS W1004. Other foundational exceptions require Committee on Instruction approval. Core Global Core, Science and Language distribution courses may also overlap, but shared Core courses cannot. Up to two additional already-approved classes may overlap two programs; substitutions should not be sought solely to create overlap. An applicable condition may span three programs. Departmental restrictions must also be observed.",
